From: Peter Strand <peter@zarquon.se>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] sep: dump SEP firmware provenance from the ADT (touchid step 5.1b)

Follow-up to patch 0003 / step 5.1. That probe showed the SEP mailbox never
answers at m1n1 time (asc_send=1, no reply at 1ms or 200ms) with the power
domain on and the mailbox live -- i.e. the SEP core is powered but not running
its ROM servicer on the m1n1 boot path. The one cheap bit that decides whether
any local fix exists is whether iBoot started the SEP for THIS boot object.

macOS on the same unit (step4) has /chosen sepfw-booted = 1. This prints, once,
the same ADT provenance for the Asahi boot:
  - /chosen sepfw-booted / sepfw-loaded / sepfw-load-at-boot
  - the SEPFW [base,size] region from /chosen/memory-map (fw blob resident?)

Decode:
  sepfw-booted = 0  -> iBoot never started the SEP on the m1n1 path; the core is
                       halted-not-started. No wake will help; only reproducing
                       iBoot's SEP-start (upstream "SEP: WIP") would.
  sepfw-booted = 1  -> iBoot booted then slept it; a wake / RTKit-hello sequence
                       is missing (neither m1n1 nor sep.rs does it) -> possibly
                       a local fix.

Debug-only, read-only ADT access, prints once from sep_init().
diff --git a/src/sep.c b/src/sep.c
index c489004..33d9f65 100644
--- a/src/sep.c
+++ b/src/sep.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "adt.h"
 #include "asc.h"
 #include "sep.h"
 #include "types.h"
@@ -28,11 +29,43 @@ static asc_dev_t *sep_asc = NULL;
 /* touchid step 5.1: emit the getrand handshake detail exactly once per boot. */
 static bool sep_dbg_done = false;
 
+/* touchid step 5.1b: did iBoot load/boot the SEP firmware on THIS boot object?
+ * On macOS (step4) /chosen sepfw-booted = 1. If it is 0 on the m1n1 boot, iBoot
+ * left the SEP not-started (nothing to answer the mailbox); if 1, it was booted
+ * then slept (a wake/hello is missing). SEPFW=[base,size] in /chosen/memory-map
+ * says whether the fw blob is even resident in RAM. Prints once. */
+static void sep_dump_provenance(void)
+{
+    int chosen = adt_path_offset(adt, "/chosen");
+    if (chosen < 0) {
+        printf("SEP: [dbg] no /chosen node in ADT\n");
+        return;
+    }
+
+    static const char *const flags[] = {"sepfw-booted", "sepfw-loaded",
+                                         "sepfw-load-at-boot"};
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < sizeof(flags) / sizeof(flags[0]); i++) {
+        u32 v;
+        if (ADT_GETPROP(adt, chosen, flags[i], &v) < 0)
+            printf("SEP: [dbg] /chosen %s = <absent>\n", flags[i]);
+        else
+            printf("SEP: [dbg] /chosen %s = %u\n", flags[i], v);
+    }
+
+    int mm = adt_path_offset(adt, "/chosen/memory-map");
+    u64 sepfw[2];
+    if (mm >= 0 && ADT_GETPROP_ARRAY(adt, mm, "SEPFW", sepfw) >= 0)
+        printf("SEP: [dbg] SEPFW region base=0x%lx size=0x%lx\n", sepfw[0], sepfw[1]);
+    else
+        printf("SEP: [dbg] SEPFW region = <absent>\n");
+}
+
 int sep_init(void)
 {
     if (!sep_asc) {
         sep_asc = asc_init("/arm-io/sep");
         printf("SEP: [dbg] asc_init(/arm-io/sep) = %p\n", sep_asc);
+        sep_dump_provenance();
     }
     if (!sep_asc)
         return -1;
